+/*
+ * ucrt_math.c: double sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan, atan2, exp, log and hypot, and float sinf, cosf, tanf, asinf,
+ * acosf, atanf, atan2f, expf and logf, that return, bit for bit, what the Windows Universal C Runtime (ucrtbase.dll,
+ * x64) returns in its default FMA3 mode.
+ * Plain C99: every fused multiply-add is an explicit fma() or fmaf() call, contraction is off, no assembly, no
+ * intrinsics, no CPU-specific code. Runs on any CPU; without hardware FMA, fma() and fmaf() come from the C library
+ * (correctly rounded).
+ *
+ * Derived from AMD AOCL-LibM, https://github.com/amd/aocl-libm-ose, commit 29fd054f383e6c5e2dec2fce781d5220059f1836:
+ *   sin, cos, tan for |x| >= pi/4 (and the kernels):  src/isa/avx2/gas/{sin,cos,tan}_fma3.S and the macros
+ *     sin_piby4_s_fma3, sin_piby4_s_xx_zero_fma3, cos_piby4_s_fma3, tan_piby4_s_fma3, tan_piby4_s_zero_fma3,
+ *     range_e_5_s_fma3, call_remainder_piby2_fma3 and the data in src/isa/avx2/include/trig_func.h,
+ *     translated instruction by instruction into C;
+ *   tan and cos for |x| < pi/4: the AOCL kernels re-expressed as fitted against UCRT (see PORT.md);
+ *   asin, acos, atan, atan2: src/ref/{asin,acos,atan,atan2}.c with explicit fma() at the sites UCRT fuses;
+ *   exp, log: src/isa/avx/gas/exp.S, src/isa/avx2/gas/log_fma3.S;
+ *   hypot: src/ref/hypot.c with UCRT's plain sum of squares;
+ *   sinf, cosf, tanf, expf: src/isa/avx2/gas/{sinf,cosf,tanf,expf}_fma3.S (sin and cos kernels with the
+ *     coefficients of src/isa/avx/gas/sinf.S); logf: src/isa/avx2/masm/logf_fma3.asm;
+ *   asinf, atanf, atan2f: src/ref/{asinf,atanf,atan2f}.c; acosf: src/ref/acosf.c as first imported (2a9b9dc6).
+ * Modifications are listed in PORT.md, each tied to a measured difference from UCRT.
+ * No Microsoft code was read; UCRT was used only as a black box to collect outputs.
+ *
+ * Original copyright notice of the AOCL-LibM files this is derived from:
+ *
+ * Copyright (C) 2008-2026 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. All rights reserved.
+ *
+ * Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification,
+ * are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:
+ * 1. Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright notice,
+ *    this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.
+ * 2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice,
+ *    this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in the documentation
+ *    and/or other materials provided with the distribution.
+ * 3. Neither the name of the copyright holder nor the names of its contributors
+ *    may be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without
+ *    specific prior written permission.
+ *
